:: Farm Woodland
<<set $outside to 1>><<set $location to "alex_farm">><<set $bus to "woodland">><<effects>>
<<farm_work_update>>

You are in the woodland within the farm grounds.
<<if $farm_work.woodland is 0>>
	Heavy branches and thick clumps of leaves litter the trails.
	<span class="red">You will not be able to forage.</span>
<<elseif $farm_work.woodland is 1>>
	Branches and leaves litter the trails.
	<span class="red">You will not be able to forage.</span>
<<elseif $farm_work.woodland is 2 and $farm.woodland is 2>>
	Only a few branches and sparse leaves cover the trails.
	You will be able to forage, <span class="yellow">although some branches may block your way.</span>
<<elseif $farm_work.woodland is 3 and $farm.woodland is 3>>
	You will be able to forage, <span class="green">and the paths through the woodland are clear.</span>
<</if>>

<<if Time.dayState is "night">>
	<<if Weather.precipitation is "snow">>
		Snow weighs down the dark boughs above.
	<<elseif Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
		The trees shield you from the icy rain.
	<<else>>
		The chill night breeze is lessened here.
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<<if Weather.precipitation is "snow">>
		Snow weighs down the boughs above.
	<<elseif Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
		The trees shield you from the worst of the rain.
	<<else>>
		You are surrounded by the chirping of birds.
	<</if>>
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<if $farm_work.pigs_out is 0>>
	<<if _farm_work_time <= -3>>
		The <<farm_text_many pig>> are asleep in their sty.
	<<elseif _farm_work_time <= 0>>
		The <<farm_text_many pig>> are rubbing each other awake.
	<<else>>
		The <<farm_text_many pig>> squeal to be let out.
	<</if>>
<<elseif $farm_work.pigs_out is 1>>
	<<if Time.season is "winter">>
		<span class="teal">The earth is too cold to find edible fungi.</span>
	<<elseif Weather.precipitation is "snow">>
		<span class="teal">The <<farm_text_many pig>> stay away from the icy treeline.</span>
	<<elseif Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
		<span class="orange">The
			<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>> pigpeople forage
			<<else>> pigs root around
			<</if>>
			in the muddy undergrowth.
		</span>
	<<else>>
		<span class="orange">The
			<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>> pigpeople forage
			<<else>>pigs root around
			<</if>>
			in the damp undergrowth.
		</span>
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<<if _farm_work_time < 46>>
		The <<farm_text_many pig>> shuffle around in their sty.
		<<if $farm_work.pig.monster is false and random(1, 2009) is 1>>
			The pigs whisper to each other about a community of angry birds deep within the woodlands. About how the birds are constructing a giant slingshot to free their brethren. The pigs sound fearful. <<stress 12>><<ggstress>>
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		The <<farm_text_many pig>> are asleep in their sty.
	<</if>>
<</if>>
<<if $farm_work.alex is "woodland">>
	Alex is removing dead wood.
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<if $stress gte 10000>>
	<<passoutfarmroad>>
<<elseif $farm_attack_timer is 0 and Time.hour gte 21>>
	<<npc Alex>><<person1>>
	Alex rushes over. <span class="red">"Remy's here,"</span> <<he>> says. "We can do this. Go get ready, I'll
	<<if $farm.tower_guard>>
		check on $farm.tower_guard."
	<<else>>
		see if I can spot them."
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<farm_assault_intro>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Prepare|Farm Assault Wardrobe]]>><<endevent>><<set $phase to 2>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<if $farm_work.alex is "woodland">>
		<<if pcAreArmsBound("both")>>
			<span class="red">Both of your arms are bound</span>, so you are unable to help Alex tend the woodland.
		<<else>>
			<<foresticon>><<link [[Help Alex tend the woodland (0:20)|Farm Woodland Tend Alex]]>><<set $farm_work.woodland += 1>><<farm_count 20>><<physique 2>><<pass 20>><<tending 2>><<tiredness 2>><<set $farm_work.tending += 1>><</link>><<gtiredness>><<gtending>>
		<</if>>
		<br>
	<<elseif $farm_work.woodland lt $farm.woodland>>
		<<if pcAreArmsBound("both")>>
			<span class="red">Both of your arms are bound</span>, so you are unable to tend the woodland.
		<<else>>
			<<foresticon>><<link [[Tend the woodland (0:20)|Farm Woodland Tend]]>><<set $farm_work.woodland += 1>><<farm_count 20>><<physique 2>><<pass 20>><<tending 2>><<tiredness 2>><<set $farm_work.tending += 1>><</link>><<gtiredness>><<gtending>>
		<</if>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<!--
		The PC can only forage AFTER the woodland has been fully tended to. Since the "Forage for fungi" activity will also be a way to raise the Pig's Respect, and upgrading the woodland increases the Pig Respect's decay, the PC will have the option to forage once per day at Woodlands Level 2, and twice per day at Woodlands Level 3.

		A Level 3 Woodland will give double the produce of a Level 2 Woodland, and need an extra 20 minutes of tending to make the activity available. If the PC doesn't want to spend that time tending, they can wait for Alex to finish it when he's doing his chores. However, the "Forage for fungi" activity will only be available while the pigs are outside of the sty.

		Using the current Market Stall rates, Foraging for Fruit with a Level 2 Woodlands will give £50 worth of fruit, while Foraging for Fungi will give £100 worth of fungi. This bonus increases up to 2x at Tending S, and up to 2.4x if the PC also has the Green Thumb trait.

		Foraging is broken up into 3 20-minute events, where a dangerEvent() may trigger each time. When Foraging for Fungi, there will be a 1/2 chance for a Pig-based Skill-Check, increased to 4/5 with a Level 3 Woodland. Passing this Skill Check will give +1 Pig's Respect.

		Foraging for Fungi will also require the PC to reward the pigs when they return to the farm, with either potatoes, carrots, apples, or their body. These options have varying pros and cons. The requested amount of food scales off of the PC's harvest, and the amounts will increase if the Pig's Respect is too low.

		If the Pig's Respect is less than -20, an extreme encounter will occur, where the pigs will first lead the PC deep into the
		woodlands so they can't call Alex for help. They will then demand a reward. The PC can reward them with their harvest, or their body. If the PC doesn't have enough food, the pigs will force the PC to reward them with their body, and the following encounters will be consensual. If the PC refuses they will be attacked, and the following encounters will be non-consensual.

		A Level 3 Woodland gives up to an average of £960 fungi after 2 hours of foraging, assuming the PC has Tending S, the Green Thumb Trait, and doesn't reward the pigs with food.
	-->
	<<if $farm_work.forage lt ($farm.woodland - 1) and $farm_work.woodland gte $farm.woodland>>
		<<if pcAreArmsBound("both")>>
			<span class="red">Both of your arms are bound</span>, so you are unable to forage.
		<<else>>
			<!-- Tiredness applied at the start of every 20 minute segment. -->
			<<foresticon "bush">><<link [[Forage for fruits (1:00)|Farm Woodland Forage]]>><<set $farm_work.forage += 1>>
				<<set $tempBasket to [0, 0, 0]>>
				<<set $tempAttempts to 3>>
				<<set $tempForageType to "fruit">>
			<</link>><<gtiredness>>
			<<if $farm_work.pigs_out is 1 and Time.season is not "winter">>
				<br>
				<<animalicon "pig">><<link [[Forage for fungi (1:00)|Farm Woodland Forage]]>><<set $farm_work.forage += 1>>
					<<set $tempBasket to [0, 0, 0]>>
					<<set $tempAttempts to 3>>
					<<set $tempForageType to "fungi">>
				<</link>><<gtiredness>>
			<</if>>
		<</if>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave (0:05)|Farm Work]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Farm Woodland Tend
<<effects>><<outfitChecks>>

You remove dead wood, and trim the branches of the wildest trees.
<br><br>

<<if dangerEvent()>>
	<!-- 0 means upper clothing, 1 means lower clothing -->
	<<set _branchTarget to random(0, 1)>>
	<<if _top>>
		<<set _top.integrity -= 10>>
		<<if _top.integrity lte 0>>
			Your _top.name <<= _top.plural ? "catch" : "catches">> on one such branch as a gust of wind disturbs it.
			<span class="pink">The force tears the fabric from your body, baring your <<undertop>>.</span>
		<<else>>
			Your _top.name <<= _top.plural ? "catch" : "catches">> on one such branch, leaving your _top.name worse for wear.
		<</if>>
	<<elseif _bottom>>
		<<set _bottom.integrity -= 10>>
		<<if _bottom.integrity lte 0>>
			Your _bottom.name <<= _bottom.plural ? "catch" : "catches">> on one such branch as a gust of wind disturbs it.
			<span class="pink">The force tears the fabric from your body, baring your <<undies>>.</span>
		<<else>>
			Your _bottom.name <<= _bottom.plural ? "catch" : "catches">> on one such branch, leaving your _bottom.name worse for wear.
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		A gust of wind animates the branches as you work, scratching your skin.<<gpain>><<pain 4>>
	<</if>>
	<<integritycheck no_text>><<exposure>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland]]>><</link>>
<</if>>


:: Farm Woodland Tend Alex
<<effects>>

<<npc Alex>><<person1>>
You help Alex remove dead wood, and trim the branches of the wildest trees.
<br><br>

<<if random(1, 4) is 4>>
	<<He>> points at the boughs above. "We'll need help to reach," <<he>> says. "I'll fetch it."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> returns a few moments later, carrying a long ladder beneath one arm. <<He>> rests it against the offending tree.

	<<if random(1, 2) is 2>>
		"The ground's uneven. You climb with the saw, and I'll steady you. Shouldn't take long."
		<br><br>

		<<if setup.clothes.lower[clothesIndex('lower', $worn.lower)].skirt is 1>>
			You climb the ladder. It wobbles a little, and you hesitate.
			<br><br>

			"You alright?" Alex says.
			<br>
			You nod, and reach for the nearest branch. You rest the saw against it, then run the metal back and forth. You pick up speed. The force reverberates through you, rocking the ladder a little.
			<br>
			A stiff breeze ruffles your skirt, brushing it against your legs.
			<br>
			You glance down, <span class="pink">and catch Alex staring right between your thighs.</span> <<His>> cheeks are red.
			<br><br>

			<<link [[Ignore|Farm Woodland Tend Alex Ignore]]>><<stress 6>><<npcincr Alex lust 10>><<arousal 1000>><</link>><<ggarousal>><<gstress>><<gglust>>
			<br>
			<<link [[Call out|Farm Woodland Tend Alex Call]]>><<stress -6>><<npcincr Alex love -1>><</link>><<llove>><<lstress>>
			<br>
			<<if hasSexStat("exhibitionism", 3)>>
				<<link [[Flaunt|Farm Woodland Tend Alex Flaunt]]>><</link>><<exhibitionist3>><<npcincr Alex lust 5>>
				<br>
			<</if>>
			<<if displayDefiantOption(500)>>
				<<link [[Taunt|Farm Woodland Tend Alex Taunt]]>><<wolfDefiant 500>><<def 1>><</link>><<npcincr Alex dom -3>><<npcincr Alex lust 5>><<defianttext 500>><<lldom>><<glust>>
				<br>
			<</if>>

		<<else>>
			You climb the ladder. It wobbles a little, and you hesitate.
			<br><br>

			"You alright?" Alex says.
			<br>
			You nod, and reach for the nearest branch. You rest the saw against it, then run the metal back and forth. You pick up speed. The force reverberates through you, rocking the ladder a little.
			<br>
			You give Alex a heads up. The branch falls to the leaf-strewn floor a moment later.
			<br><br>

			"Thanks for the help," Alex says as you reach the bottom.
			<br><br>

			<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
			<br>
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		"The ground's uneven. Could you hold the ladder while I climb? It shouldn't take long."
		<br><br>

		You stand at the base of the ladder as <<he>> climbs.
		<<if $pronoun is "f">>
			You wouldn't need to lean much to see up <<his>> skirt.
			<br><br>

			<<set $skulduggerydifficulty to 700>>
			<<link [[Peek|Farm Woodland Tend Skirt]]>><<arousal 600>><</link>><<skulduggerydifficulty>><<garousal>>
			<br>
			<<link [[Don't peek|Farm Woodland Tend No Skirt]]>><<npcincr Alex love 1>><</link>>
			<br>
		<<else>>
			You keep your face down to shield yourself from the splinters. "Here it comes," <<he>> says. The branch falls to the leaf-strewn floor a moment later.
			<br><br>

			"Thanks for the help," Alex says as <<he>> reaches the bottom.<<glove>><<npcincr Alex love 1>>
			<br><br>

			<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<</if>>


:: Farm Woodland Tend Skirt
<<effects>>

You step around the ladder just as a gust billows Alex's skirt, giving you a clear view of <<his>> red boyshorts.
<br><br>

<<skulduggerycheck>>
<<if $skulduggerysuccess is 1>>

	<<He>> doesn't notice your gaze. You continue stealing peeks as Alex saws the branch. "Here it comes," <<he>> says. The branch thuds to the leaf-strewn floor beside you. "Coming down."
	<br><br>

	<<skulduggeryuse>>

	"Thanks for the help," <<he>> says once down.<<glove>><<npcincr Alex love 1>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

<<else>>

	<<He>> glances down, <span class="red">and yelps.</span> <<He>> pushes <<his>> skirt between <<his>> thighs with one hand, and almost falls from the ladder.<<llove>><<gglust>><<npcincr Alex love -1>><<npcincr Alex lust 10>>
	<br><br>

	"D-don't look," <<he>> says.

	<<skulduggeryuse>>

	<<link [[Apologise|Farm Woodland Tend Apologise]]>><<npcincr Alex love 1>><<stress 6>><</link>><<gstress>><<glove>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Tease|Farm Woodland Tend Tease]]>><<npcincr Alex dom 1>><</link>><<promiscuous1>><<gdom>>

<</if>>


:: Farm Woodland Tend Apologise
<<effects>>

<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
	"I-I'm so sorry," you say, averting your eyes. "I didn't mean to look."
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	"Yeah, that was classless of me," you say, averting your eyes. "Sorry."
<<else>>
	"Sorry," you say, averting your eyes. "That was rude of me."
<</if>>
<br><br>

"Just don't look again," Alex says. <<He>> saws through the log, but keeps <<his>> legs together until <<hes>> finished.
<br><br>

<<Hes>> still blushing when the branch falls to the floor, and <<he>> climbs back down.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland]]>><<endevent>><</link>>


:: Farm Woodland Tend Tease
<<effects>>

<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
	"C-cute underwear," you giggle.
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	"Nice underwear," you tease. "Shame to hide it."
<<else>>
	"You've good taste in underwear," you say.
<</if>>
<<promiscuity1>>

Alex's blush deepens. <<He>> continues sawing the log, but keeps <<his>> legs tight together, <<his>> skirt bunched between them, until <<hes>> finished.
<br><br>

<<Hes>> still blushing when the branch falls to the floor, and <<he>> climbs back down.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland]]>><<endevent>><</link>>


:: Farm Woodland Tend No Skirt
<<effects>>

You look away as Alex saws through the branch. "Here it comes," <<he>> says. It thuds to the leaf-strewn floor a moment later.
<br><br>

"Thanks for the help," <<he>> says as <<he>> reaches the bottom.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland]]>><<endevent>><</link>>


:: Farm Woodland Forage
<<effects>>
<<farm_work_update>>

<!-- Check for if the PC will get the Extreme treatment. -->
<<if $tempExtreme is undefined>>
	<<if $farm.beasts.pigs gte -20>>
		<<set $tempExtreme to false>>
	<<else>>
		<<set $tempExtreme to true>>
	<</if>>
<</if>>

<<farm_gen pig>>

<<set $tempAttempts -= 1>>
<<if $tempAttempts lt 0>>
	<!-- Triggers at the end of the foraging session -->
	<<if $tempForageType is "fruit" or not $tempExtreme>>
		You can see the treeline from here.

		<<set _uniqueItems to 0>>
		<<for $_i = 0; $_i lt $tempBasket.length; $_i++>>
			<<if $tempBasket[$_i] gt 0>>
				<<set _uniqueItems += 1>>
			<</if>>
		<</for>>
		<<if $tempForageType is "fruit">>
			<<set _basketTypes to ["strawberry", "peach", "plum"]>>
			You have found
			<span class="green">
				<<set _uniqueCounter to 0>>
				<<for $_j = 0; $_j < 3; $_j++>>
					<<if $tempBasket[$_j] gt 0>>
						<<set _uniqueCounter += 1>>
						<<if _uniqueItems is 1>>
							<<foodstuffReport _basketTypes[$_j] $tempBasket[$_j] _basketTypes[$_j]>>.
						<<elseif _uniqueCounter is _uniqueItems>>
							and <<foodstuffReport _basketTypes[$_j] $tempBasket[$_j] _basketTypes[$_j]>>.
						<<else>>
							<<foodstuffReport _basketTypes[$_j] $tempBasket[$_j] _basketTypes[$_j]>>,
						<</if>>
					<</if>>
				<</for>>
			</span>
			<br><br>

			<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland]]>>
				<<endWoodlandForage>>
			<</link>>
			<br>
		<<elseif $tempForageType is "fungi">>
			<<set _basketTypes to ["mushroom", "truffle", ""]>>
			You have found
			<span class="green">
				<<if _uniqueItems is 1>>
					<<for $_j = 0; $_j < 2; $_j++>>
						<<if $tempBasket[$_j] gt 0>>
							<<foodstuffReport _basketTypes[$_j] $tempBasket[$_j] _basketTypes[$_j]>>.
						<</if>>
					<</for>>
				<<else>>
					<<foodstuffReport "mushroom" $tempBasket[0] "mushroom">>, and <<foodstuffReport "truffle" $tempBasket[1] "truffle">>.
				<</if>>
			</span>
			<br><br>

			<!--
				The base foraging rates will require you to reward £100.00 of fungi with £8.00 of potatoes, £10.00 of carrots, or £5.00 of apples. This assumes apples can only be harvested in the Forest. Quantities may need to be changed if apples suddenly become easier to harvest.

				The requested quantity is increased by 2x if the Pig's Respect is between -20 and -6.
			-->
			<<if $farm.beasts.pigs gte -5>>
				<<set _respectModifier to 1>>
				The <<farm_text_many pig>> crowd around you.
				<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>"Reward?" "Helpful?" "Food?" "Reward?" They ask.
				<<else>>They bump you with their snouts, asking for a reward.
				<</if>>
				While you could also give them nothing, you get the feeling that refusing too often may be a <span class="red">very bad idea.</span>
			<<else>>
				<<set _respectModifier to 2>>
				The <<farm_text_many pig>> crowd around you. They jostle you around, insisting on a large reward. While you could also give them nothing, you get the feeling that refusing any more <span class="red">will be a very bad idea.</span>
			<</if>>
			<br><br>

			<!--
				Truffles are significantly more expensive than mushrooms. To prevent truffles from being weighted much more heavily than mushrooms in the request calculations, the Pig's requests are adjusted according to the QUANTITY of each item that's been collected, scaled by the average value the PC expects to make each hour.
			-->
			<<set _averageValue to (2 * setup.foodstuff["mushroom"].shop.sell_price
				+ 1 * setup.foodstuff["truffle"].shop.sell_price) / 3>>
			<!-- Units are in hundredths of a pound. Quantities will be rounded up because pigs are greedy. -->
			<<set _requestedValue to $tempBasket[0] * _averageValue + $tempBasket[1] * _averageValue>>

			<!-- Requires 8% of the market value in potatoes. -->
			<<set _requiredPotatoes to Math.ceil((_requestedValue * 0.08 * _respectModifier)
				/ setup.foodstuff["potato"].shop.sell_price)>>
			<!-- Or, 10% of the market value in carrots. -->
			<<set _requiredCarrots to Math.ceil((_requestedValue * 0.10 * _respectModifier)
				/ setup.foodstuff["wild_carrot"].shop.sell_price)>>
			<!-- Or, 5% of the market value in apples. -->
			<<set _requiredApples to Math.ceil((_requestedValue * 0.05 * _respectModifier)
				/ setup.foodstuff["apple"].shop.sell_price)>>

			<<if $farm_work.pigs_fed gte 6>>
				<<foodstufficon "potato">><span class="blue">The pigs are too full to want more potatoes.</span>
			<<elseif $foodstuff["potato"].amount gte _requiredPotatoes>>
				<<foodstufficon "potato">><<link [[Reward them with potatoes (0:20)|Farm Woodland Forage Reward]]>>
					<<set $tempRewardType to "potato">>
					<<set $tempRewardQuantity to _requiredPotatoes>>
					<<set $foodstuff["potato"].amount -= _requiredPotatoes>>
				<</link>>
			<<else>>
				<<insufficientQuantity "potatoes to satisfy them" "blue" "<<foodstufficon 'potato'>>">>
			<</if>>
			<br>

			<<if $foodstuff["wild_carrot"].amount gte _requiredCarrots>>
				<<foodstufficon "wild_carrot">><<link [[Reward them with carrots (0:10)|Farm Woodland Forage Reward]]>>
					<<set $tempRewardType to "carrot">>
					<<set $tempRewardQuantity to _requiredCarrots>>
					<<set $foodstuff["wild_carrot"].amount -= _requiredCarrots>>
				<</link>>
			<<else>>
				<<insufficientQuantity "carrots to satisfy them" "blue" "<<foodstufficon 'wild_carrot'>>">>
			<</if>>
			<br>

			<<if $foodstuff["apple"].amount gte _requiredApples>>
				<<if currentSkillValue("housekeeping") gte 400 and $mathstrait gte 3>>
					<<foodstufficon "apple">><<link [[Reward them with apples (0:20)|Farm Woodland Forage Reward]]>>
						<<set $tempRewardType to "apple">>
						<<set $tempRewardQuantity to _requiredApples>>
						<<set $foodstuff["apple"].amount -= _requiredApples>>
					<</link>>
				<<elseif currentSkillValue("housekeeping") gte 400>>
					<<foodstufficon "apple">><<link [[Reward them with apples (0:15)|Farm Woodland Forage Reward]]>>
						<<set $tempRewardType to "apple">>
						<<set $tempRewardQuantity to _requiredApples>>
						<<set $foodstuff["apple"].amount -= _requiredApples>>
					<</link>>
				<<else>>
					<<foodstufficon "apple">><<link [[Reward them with apples (0:10)|Farm Woodland Forage Reward]]>>
						<<set $tempRewardType to "apple">>
						<<set $tempRewardQuantity to _requiredApples>>
						<<set $foodstuff["apple"].amount -= _requiredApples>>
					<</link>>
				<</if>>
			<<else>>
				<<insufficientQuantity "apples to satisfy them" "blue" "<<foodstufficon 'apple'>>">>
			<</if>>
			<br>

			<<if ($settings.bestialityEnabled or $farm_work.pig.monster) and hasSexStat("deviancy", 5)>>
				<<animalicon "pig">><<link [[Reward them with your body|Farm Woodland Forage Reward]]>>
					<<set $tempRewardType to "body">>
				<</link>><<deviant5>>
			<</if>>
			<br>

			<<getouticon>><<link [[Reward them with nothing|Farm Woodland Forage Reward]]>>
				<<set $tempRewardType to "nothing">>
			<</link>><<llrespect>>
			<br>
		<<else>>
			ERROR (Farm Woodland Forage): forageType is invalid. Please report.
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		<!--
			A PC with Tending S, the Green Thumb trait, and a Level 3 Woodland will find an average of:
			20 * 3 * 2.4 = 144 fungi.

			Once the Pig's Respect is less than -20, they will take the PC deep into the woodland at the end of the foraging session, and demand a reward. The PC will have the option to give them their harvest, reward them with their body, or refuse.

			The pigs will initially want to have sex with the PC 4 times. If the PC offers them their harvest, each "attempt" will eat up a random (20 to 40) amount of fungi from the PC's basket, repeating 5 times (150 fungi on average). Each fully satisfied attempt will reduce the number of pigs by 1. If the pigs can eat their fill at least 4 times, they will leave the PC alone.

			If the pigs can eat their fill 5 times, they will leave the PC with whatever food is left over, then rest and head back to the farm.

			Each fully satisfied pig gives +1 Pig's Respect (+4 max).

			Pigs will eat the truffles first, then the mushrooms.

			If the PC refuses, the number of attempts will increase by 1 to a total of 5, and all remaining encounters will become non-consensual.
		-->
		You've been here for a while. You decide to count up your harvest, then head back towards the farm.

		<<set _uniqueItems to 0>>
		<<for $_i = 0; $_i lt $tempBasket.length; $_i++>>
			<<if $tempBasket[$_i] gt 0>>
				<<set _uniqueItems += 1>>
			<</if>>
		<</for>>

		<<set _basketTypes to ["mushroom", "truffle", ""]>>
		You have found
		<span class="green">
			<<if _uniqueItems is 1>>
				<<for $_j = 0; $_j < 2; $_j++>>
					<<if $tempBasket[$_j] gt 0>>
						<<foodstuffReport _basketTypes[$_j] $tempBasket[$_j] _basketTypes[$_j]>>.
					<</if>>
				<</for>>
			<<else>>
				<<foodstuffReport "mushroom" $tempBasket[0] "mushroom">>, and <<foodstuffReport "truffle" $tempBasket[1] "truffle">>.
			<</if>>
		</span>
		<br><br>

		You look around. You don't recognize this area of the woods. Something isn't right...
		<br><br>

		<!-- The farm_gen chain of doom -->
		A <<farm_text pig>> pokes <<farm_his pig>> head out from behind a tree.
		<<farm_gen pig>>
		Another <<farm_text pig>> walks out from a bush.
		<<farm_gen pig>>
		Another <<farm_text pig>> appears behind you.
		<<farm_gen pig>>
		Another <<farm_text pig>> pushes through a thicket.
		<<farm_gen pig>>
		You see another <<farm_text pig>>.
		And then another. And another. And another. And another. <span class="red">And another. And another.</span>
		<br><br>

		The <<farm_text_many pig>> surround you.

		<<farm_gen pig>>
		<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
			One of the <<farm_text_many pig>> speaks up. "We help you. Many time. You give reward. Now."
		<<else>>
			They stare at your basket. You think the implication is clear.
		<</if>>
		<br><br>

		<<if $rentmoney gt $money>>
			You think about giving them your harvest, but you're barely scraping by. Can you really afford it?
		<<elseif $rentmoney * 2 gt $money>>
			You think about giving them your harvest, but money is tight. Can you still make enough for next week?
		<<else>>
			You think about giving them your harvest. All things considered, you can afford to lose some
			<<if $tempBasket[0] gt 0>> mushrooms.
			<<else>> truffles.
			<</if>>
		<</if>>
		<<if hasSexStat("deviancy", 5)>> You could offer them your body, but how many times will you need to satisfy them?<</if>>
		<br><br>

		<<foodstufficon "mushroom">><<link [[Offer your harvest (?:??)|Farm Woodland Forage Reward Extreme]]>>
			<<set $tempRewardType to "basket">>
		<</link>>
		<br>

		<!-- The "body" and "nothing" rewards are disabled when bestiality is disabled and the pigs aren't monsters. -->
		<<if $settings.bestialityEnabled or $farm_work.pig.monster>>
			<<if hasSexStat("deviancy", 5)>>
				<<animalicon "pig">><<link [[Offer your body (?:??)|Farm Woodland Forage Reward Extreme]]>>
					<<set $tempRewardType to "body">>
				<</link>><<deviant5>>
			<</if>>
			<br>

			<<foresticon>><<link [[Refuse (?:??)|Farm Woodland Forage Reward Extreme]]>>
				<<set $tempRewardType to "nothing">>
			<</link>><<dangerousText>>
			<br>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<<pass 20>>
	<<tiredness 2>>

	<<if $tempForageType is "fruit">> <<outfitChecks>>
	<<else>> <<pigsOpinion>>
	<</if>>

	<<if $tempForageType is "fruit">>
		You take a basket into the woodland, and search the boughs and bushes for fruit.
	<<elseif $tempForageType is "fungi">>
		You take a basket into the woodland, and search the undergrowth for fungi.
		<<if not $tempExtreme>>
			The <<farm_text_many pig>> guide you along.
		<<else>>
			<span class="red">The <<farm_text_many pig>> guide you along.</span>
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		ERROR (Farm Woodland Forage): forageType is invalid. Please report.
	<</if>>
	<<physique 1>>
	<br><br>

	<!--
		The PC makes 3 foraging checks, each taking 20 minutes, with a chance of receiving ANY type of fruit.

		Pig-based dangerEvents may trigger if the PC is Foraging for Fungi.

		Basket holds Strawberries, Peaches, and Plums when Foraging for Fruit, or Mushrooms and Truffles when Foraging for Fungi.
	-->
	<<if $tempForageType is "fruit">>
		<<set _target to random(0, 2)>>
		<<switch _target>>
			<<case 0>>
				<!-- Strawberries -->
				<<wearProp "strawberry basket">>
				<span class="green">You find some ripe <<foodstufficon "strawberry">> strawberries.</span>
				<<if $farm.woodland gte 3>>
					<<tending_pick strawberry 20 50>>
				<<else>>
					<<tending_pick strawberry 10 25>>
				<</if>>
				<<set $tempBasket[0] += _tending_amount>>
			<<case 1>>
				<!-- Peaches -->
				<<wearProp "peach basket">>
				<span class="green">You find some ripe <<foodstufficon "peach">> peaches.</span>
				<<if $farm.woodland gte 3>>
					<<tending_pick peach 10 40>>
				<<else>>
					<<tending_pick peach 5 20>>
				<</if>>
				<<set $tempBasket[1] += _tending_amount>>
			<<case 2>>
				<!-- Plums -->
				<<wearProp "plum basket">>
				<span class="green">You find some ripe <<foodstufficon "plum">> plums.</span>
				<<if $farm.woodland gte 3>>
					<<tending_pick plum 20 40>>
				<<else>>
					<<tending_pick plum 10 20>>
				<</if>>
				<<set $tempBasket[2] += _tending_amount>>
		<</switch>>
	<<elseif $tempForageType is "fungi">>
		<!-- When foraging for fungi, there is a 2/3 chance to find Mushrooms, and a 1/3 chance to find Truffles -->
		<<set _target to random(1, 3)>>
		<!--
			For calculation purposes, the exact quantities and frequencies that the Mushrooms and Truffles are harvested at should stay equal to each other if they end up being adjusted. Otherwise, the _averageValue variable will need to be recalculated with the new rates in mind.
		-->
		<<if _target lte 2>>
			<!-- Mushrooms -->
			<<wearProp "mushroom basket">>
			<span class="green">You find some <<foodstufficon "mushroom">> mushrooms.</span>
			<<if $farm.woodland gte 3>>
				<<tending_pick mushroom 10 30>>
			<<else>>
				<<tending_pick mushroom 5 15>>
			<</if>>
			<<set $tempBasket[0] += _tending_amount>>
		<<else>>
			<!-- Truffles -->
			<!-- NOTE: THERE DOES NOT CURRENTLY EXIST A TRUFFLE BASKET SPRITE. SPRITEWORK NEEDED. -->
			<<wearProp "mushroom basket">>
			<span class="green">You find some <<foodstufficon "truffle">> truffles.</span>
			<<if $farm.woodland gte 3>>
				<<tending_pick truffle 10 30>>
			<<else>>
				<<tending_pick truffle 5 15>>
			<</if>>
			<<set $tempBasket[1] += _tending_amount>>
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		ERROR (Farm Woodland Forage): forageType is invalid. Please report.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<!--
		If the PC is foraging for fruit or disabled bestiality, they will get scratched by some branches and nothing else will happen.

		If they are foraging for fungi with a Level 2 Woodland, they will have a 1/2 chance of getting molested by a pig after being scratched by a branch.

		If they are foraging for fungi with a Level 3 Woodland, they will have a 4/5 chance of getting molested by a pig.

		If the chosen target on the PC's body fails, or if the PC gets hit with an unlucky 1/4, the pig will simply tackle them and the skill checks will be harder.
	-->
	<<if ($tempForageType is "fruit" and dangerEvent()) or ($tempForageType is "fungi" and (_fullyNaked or dangerEvent(1.25)))>>
		<<set _checkResults to [
			$hairlength gte random(300, 500),
			not _topless,
			not _bottomless,
		]>>
		<<set _attemptOne to random(0, 2)>>

		<<if _attemptOne is 0 and _checkResults[_attemptOne]>>
			Your <<hairDetails>> catches on a branch as a gust of wind disturbs it. It's stuck.<<gpain>><<pain 4>>
		<<elseif _attemptOne is 1 and _checkResults[_attemptOne]>>
			<<set _top.integrity -= 10>>
			<<if _top.integrity lte 0>>
				Your _top.name <<= _top.plural ? "catch" : "catches">> on a branch as a gust of wind disturbs it.
				<span class="pink">The force tears the fabric from your body, baring your <<undertop>>.</span>
			<<else>>
				Your _top.name <<= _top.plural ? "catch" : "catches">> on a branch, leaving your _top.name worse for wear.
			<</if>>
		<<elseif _attemptOne is 2 and _checkResults[_attemptOne]>>
			<<set _bottom.integrity -= 10>>
			<<if _bottom.integrity lte 0>>
				Your _bottom.name <<= _bottom.plural ? "catch" : "catches">> on a branch as a gust of wind disturbs it.
				<span class="pink">The force tears the fabric from your body, baring your <<undies>>.</span>
			<<else>>
				Your _bottom.name <<= _bottom.plural ? "catch" : "catches">> on a branch, leaving your _bottom.name worse for wear.
			<</if>>
		<<else>>
			A gust of wind animates the nearby branches, scratching your skin.<<gpain>><<pain 4>>
		<</if>>
		<<integritycheck no_text>><<exposure>>
		<br><br>

		<<if $tempForageType is "fungi"
			and (($farm.woodland is 2 and random(1, 2) is 2) or ($farm.woodland is 3 and random(1, 5) lte 4))
			and ($settings.bestialityEnabled or $farm_work.pig.monster)>>
			<!--
				The event will be initiated by the PC's hair or clothes catching on a branch. Upon triggering this event, a pig will try to molest them.

				If however the targeted check fails, due to the PC's hair being too short, the PC's upper or lower clothing slot being naked, or they simply hit the unlucky 1/4, the pig will first tackle them and the skill checks will be harder.
			-->
			<<if _checkResults[_attemptOne] and random(1, 4) is not 1>>
				<<if _attemptOne is 0>>
					As you untangle your hair,
				<<else>>
					<!-- Player's body is targeted while they're wearing clothes. -->
					As you untangle yourself,
				<</if>>

				<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
					a <<farm_text pig>> grasps your <<hairDetails>> and tries to force you to the ground.
				<<else>>
					a pig rears on its hind legs and tries to force you to the ground.
				<</if>>
				<br><br>

				<<link [[Scold|Farm Woodland Pigs Scold]]>>
					<<set $tempPosition to "standing">>
				<</link>><<tendingdifficulty 1 1000>>
				<br>
				<<link [[Shove <<farm_him pig>> away|Farm Woodland Pigs Shove]]>>
					<<set $tempPosition to "standing">>
				<</link>><<physiquedifficulty 1 12000>>
				<br>
				<<link [[Endure|Farm Woodland Pigs Endure]]>><<farm_pigs -1>><<trauma 6>><<stress 6>>
					<<set $tempPosition to "standing">>
				<</link>><<lrespect>><<gtrauma>><<gstress>>
				<br>
				<<if hasSexStat("deviancy", 3)>>
					<<link [[Give <<farm_him pig>> a hand|Farm Woodland Pigs Hand]]>>
						<<set $sexstart to 1>>
						<<set $tempPosition to "standing">>
					<</link>><<deviant3>>
					<br>
				<</if>>
			<<else>>
				<<if _attemptOne is 0 and _checkResults[_attemptOne]>>
					As you untangle your hair,
				<<elseif (_attemptOne is 1 or _attemptOne is 2) and _checkResults[_attemptOne]>>
					As you untangle yourself,
				<<else>>
					<!-- Failed the check. -->
					As you back away from the branches,
				<</if>>
				you trip on a root and fall onto your back. Looking up, you see a <<farm_text pig>> standing in front of you. Emboldened by your vulnerability, <<farm_he pig>> tries to mount you.
				<br><br>

				<!-- Exact position is "missionary". -->
				<<link [[Scold|Farm Woodland Pigs Scold]]>>
					<<set $tempPosition to "prone">>
				<</link>><<tendingdifficulty 1 1300>>
				<br>
				<<link [[Shove <<farm_him pig>> away|Farm Woodland Pigs Shove]]>>
					<<set $tempPosition to "prone">>
				<</link>><<physiquedifficulty 1 16000>>
				<br>
				<!-- Enduring not possible because the PC is already prone. -->
				<<if hasSexStat("deviancy", 4)>>
					<<link [[Give <<farm_him pig>> a hand|Farm Woodland Pigs Hand]]>>
						<<set $sexstart to 1>>
						<<set $tempPosition to "prone">>
					<</link>><<deviant4>>
					<br>
				<</if>>
			<</if>>
		<<else>>
			<<link [[Continue|Farm Woodland Forage]]>><</link>>
		<</if>>

	<<else>>
		<!--
			Ok ok. Hear me out. *Dons tinfoil hat* WHAT IF. Huamns are not the only ones who gain benefits from using the Strange Flowers? WHAT IF. Animals who eat them gain a minor boost to their intelligence, and increased lust towards humans? WHAT IF. The pigs on Alex's Farm started eating these after being let into the Woodland, WHICH ENDED UP MAKING THEM SMARTER?!!?? AM I COOKING?!?! DO WE COOK THESE??!!??
		-->
		<<if random(1, 5) is 1>>
			You smell a mesmerising sweetness. It leads you to a patch of strange purple flowers.
			<br><br>
			<<if pcAreArmsBound("both")>>
				<!-- Shouldn't currently be possible to reach this text, as you can't start foraging if your arms are
					bound. Maybe there will be an arm binding event in the future? -->
				<span class="red">Both of your arms are bound</span>, so you are unable to pick the flower.
				<br>
			<<else>>
				<<foodstufficon "strange_flower">><<link [[Pick|Farm Woodland Strange Harvest]]>><<drugs 60>><</link>><<garousal>>
			<</if>>
			<br>
			<<getouticon>><<link [[Ignore|Farm Woodland Forage]]>><</link>>
			<br>

		<<else>>
			<<link [[Continue|Farm Woodland Forage]]>><</link>>
			<br>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
<</if>>


<!-- rewardType can be "basket", "body", or "nothing" -->
<!--
	Reward Tradeoffs:
	Basket
		Pros:
			Reduces the number of pigs the PC needs to have sex with.
			With enough mushrooms, the sex can be avoided entirely.
			Each satisfied pig gives +1 Respect.
		Cons:
			The pigs demand a LOT of mushrooms.
			The number of pigs is only decreased for each pig that is FULLY satisfied.
	Body
		Pros:
			Pigs will not steal from your basket while you're having sex.
			Each satisfied pig gives +1 Respect. Passing a bonus Tending and Science check will let the PC get an additional +1 Respect.
			Gives the maximum amount of Pig's Respect (+5)
			You are having sex with pigs.
		Cons:
			You are having sex with pigs.
	Nothing
		Pros:
			Encounters will all be non-consensual. You're such a go go getter lmao
			Each pig fought off gives +1 Respect.
			This option can also give the maximum amount of Pig's Respect (By fighting off 5 pigs).
		Cons:
			Pigs will steal from your basket while you're being molested.
			You will have to fight off 5 pigs.
-->
:: Farm Woodland Forage Reward Extreme
<<effects>><<outfitChecks>>

<<if $tempRewardType is "basket">>
	You hold out your basket. The <<farm_text_many pig>> stare at it.
	<br><br>

	<<farm_gen pig>>

	<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
		"I hope this is enough for you." You start handing out your mushrooms. "Eep!" But a <<farm_text pig>> knocks the basket out of your hands.
		<!-- Lillia transformation when? Plz I need -->
		<<if $tempBasket[1] gt 0>>They dig through the spilled contents, seeming to like your truffles.
		<<else>>They dig into the spilled contents, pulling back after grabbing a mouthful of mushroom.
		<</if>>
	<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
		You stare back at them. They stare back at you. Finally, you slouch. "Ugh. Fine." You dump your basket onto the grass.
		<<if $tempBasket[1] gt 0>>They start picking through your harvest, seeming to like your truffles.
		<<else>>They start picking out what they like, taking away your mushrooms one by one.
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		"Is this enough?" you ask them. You pour out your harvest in front of them.
		<<if $tempBasket[1] gt 0>>They consider it, then start grabbing from the spread. They like your truffles.
		<<else>>They consider it, then start grabbing from the spread. The largest mushrooms are the first to go.
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<set _pigsUnsatisfied to -1>>
	<<for $_i = 0; $_i < 5; $_i++>>
		<<set _amountTaken to random(20, 40)>>
		<!-- Take from truffles if they exist -->
		<<if $tempBasket[1] gt 0 and $tempBasket[1] gte _amountTaken>>
			<<set $tempBasket[1] -= _amountTaken>>
			<<set $foodstuff["truffle"].amount -= _amountTaken>>
			<<set _amountTaken to 0>>
		<!-- Empty the truffles if there aren't enough -->
		<<elseif $tempBasket[1] gt 0 and $tempBasket[1] lt _amountTaken>>
			<<set _amountTaken to _amountTaken - $tempBasket[1]>>
			<<set $foodstuff["truffle"].amount -= $tempBasket[1]>>
			<<set $tempBasket[1] to 0>>
		<</if>>

		<!--
			Take from mushrooms if they exist.

			Can use an "if" statement instead of an "elseif" here because the pig will either be fully satisfied by the truffles (0), or the truffles will run out and cause the pig to look for mushrooms instead (> 0)
		-->
		<<if $tempBasket[0] gt 0 and $tempBasket[0] gte _amountTaken>>
			<<set $tempBasket[0] -= _amountTaken>>
			<<set $foodstuff["mushroom"].amount -= _amountTaken>>
			<<set _amountTaken to 0>>
		<<elseif $tempBasket[0] gt 0 and $tempBasket[0] lt _amountTaken>>
			<<set _amountTaken to _amountTaken - $tempBasket[0]>>
			<<set $foodstuff["mushroom"].amount -= $tempBasket[0]>>
			<<set $tempBasket[0] to 0>>
		<</if>>

		<!-- Check if the pig was fully satisfied. -->
		<<if _amountTaken gt 0>>
			<<set _pigsUnsatisfied += 1>>
		<<else>>
			<!-- Each serving of fungi takes the pigs ~2 minutes to eat. -->
			<<pass 2>>
		<</if>>
	<</for>>

	<!--
		Players who've disabled bestiality can only get a little respect. Failing to satisfy the pigs will instead give them increasing amounts of trauma, stress, and pain.

		The pigs will take 30-40 minutes to return to the farm from where they took the player.
	-->
	<<if _pigsUnsatisfied lte 0 or not ($settings.bestialityEnabled or $farm_work.pig.monster)>>
		<<set _passTime to random(30, 40)>>
		<<pass _passTime>>

		<<if _pigsUnsatisfied lte 0>>
			<<pass 10>>
			After some time, the <<farm_text_many pig>> laze on the earth, satisfied with the meal.
			<<if $settings.bestialityEnabled or $farm_work.pig.monster>>
				<<ggrespect>><<farm_pigs 4>>
			<<else>>
				<<grespect>><<farm_pigs 1>>
			<</if>>
			<br><br>

			<<if $tempBasket[0] + $tempBasket[1] gt 0>>
				You pick up your basket. It seems like they left some food behind. After picking up their leftovers, you're able to find
				<span class="green">
					<<if _uniqueItems is 1>>
						<<for $_j = 0; $_j < 2; $_j++>>
							<<if $tempBasket[$_j] gt 0>>
								<<foodstuffReport _basketTypes[$_j] $tempBasket[$_j] _basketTypes[$_j]>>.
							<</if>>
						<</for>>
					<<else>>
						<<foodstuffReport "mushroom" $tempBasket[0] "mushroom">>, and <<foodstuffReport "truffle" $tempBasket[1] "truffle">>.
					<</if>>
				</span>
			<</if>>
			<br><br>

			You don't know the way back, so you wait for them to get up. Some <<farm_text_many pig>> approach you during this time, giving you a lick or a nuzzle for the meal.
			<<if $settings.bestialityEnabled or $farm_work.pig.monster>>
				A few of them still look at you with lustful eyes, but the others form a ring of sorts that stops them from approaching.
			<</if>>
			<br><br>

		<span class="red">It seems like they think you've paid your due.</span><<stress 6>><<gstress>>
		<br><br>

			<<farm_gen pig>>

			<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
				"Thank meal," a <<farm_text pig>> says. "We go back now." You follow them.
			<<else>>
				Eventually, they get up and start trotting somewhere. You follow them.
			<</if>>
			<br><br>
		<<elseif _pigsUnsatisfied lte 2>>
			<!--
				Should only be possible if bestiality is disabled and the pigs aren't monsters.

				Text for 1-2 unsatisfied pigs.
			-->
			<<pass 4>>
			Once your basket is empty, some <<farm_text_many pig>> lay on the earth, satisfied with their meal.
			<br><br>

			You don't know the way back, so you wait for them to get up. A few <<farm_text_many pig>> approach you during this time, giving you a lick or a nuzzle as thanks. However, some of the <<farm_text_many pig>> seem unsatisfied. They push you around, checking if you have any more food hidden away.<<gtrauma>><<gstress>>
			<!--
				This amount includes the "It seems they think you've paid your due" stress, and adds +6 stress for every unsatisfied pig.
			-->
			<<trauma 6>>
			<<if _pigsUnsatisfied is 1>><<stress 12>>
			<<else>><<stress 18>>
			<</if>>
			<br><br>

			Eventually, they get up and start trotting somewhere. You follow them.
			<br><br>
		<<else>>
			<!--
				Should only be possible if bestiality is disabled and the pigs aren't monsters.

				Text for 3-4 unsatisfied pigs.
			-->
			<<pass 2>>
			Once your basket is empty, a few of the <<farm_text_many pig>> lay down. However, most of them are unsatisfied.
			<br><br>

			You don't know the way back, and you're worried about disturbing them, so you sit with your back against a tree. The <<farm_text_many pig>> get back up. However, instead of dispersing, they turn to you. <span class="red">They want more food.</span>
			<br><br>

			<!--
				Pigs will tear off player's clothes looking for more food. However, they will not try to molest the player.
			-->
			They knock you around, searching for anything you might have hidden away.
			<<if _top or _bottom>>
				They grasp and tear, and soon have your <span class="pink">clothes reduced to tatters.</span>
				<<clothesruined>>
				<<pain 6>>
			<<else>>
				You trip and stumble as you're shoved, scraping your skin against the nearby trees.
				<<pain 12>>
			<</if>>
			<<trauma 12>>
			<<if _pigsUnsatisfied is 3>><<stress 24>>
			<<else>><<stress 30>>
			<</if>>
			<<ggtrauma>><<ggstress>><<gpain>>
			<br><br>

			Eventually, they tire of their search, trotting away with a huff. You watch their outlines fade between the trees. Hesitantly, you follow them.
			<br><br>
		<</if>>

		<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland]]>>
			<<endWoodlandForage>>
		<</link>>
		<br>
	<<else>>
		<!-- Should only be possible if bestiality is enabled, or the pigs are monsters. -->
		<<if _pigsUnsatisfied is 1>>
			After emptying your basket, most of the <<farm_text_many pig>> laze on the earth, satisfied with their meal.
			<<farm_pigs 3>><<ggrespect>>
			<br><br>

			You don't know the way back, so you wait for them to get up. Some <<farm_text_many pig>> approach you during this time, giving you a lick or a nuzzle as thanks. However, a few of the <<farm_text_many pig>> seem unsatisfied. They walk up to you in a small group, intent on something more.
			<br><br>

			<<farm_gen pig>>

			<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
				"Not be rough," one of the <<farm_text_many pig>> says. "You give good food."
			<<else>>
				The others glance at them, then go back to lazing around.
			<</if>>
			<br><br>

		<<elseif _pigsUnsatisfied is 2 or _pigsUnsatisfied is 3>>
			Once your basket is empty, some <<farm_text_many pig>> lay on the earth, satisfied with their meal.
			<<if _pigsUnsatisfied is 2>><<farm_pigs 2>><<else>><<farm_pigs 1>><</if>>
			<<grespect>>
			<br><br>

			You don't know the way back, so you wait for them to get up. A few <<farm_text_many pig>> approach you during this
			time, giving you a lick or a nuzzle as thanks. However, some of the <<farm_text_many pig>> seem unsatisfied. They
			circle around you, intent on something more.
			<br><br>

			<<farm_gen pig>>

			<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
				"Not give enough," a <<farm_text pig>> says. "But okay. We less hungry."
			<<else>>
				The others glance at them, watching how you react.
			<</if>>
			<br><br>

		<<else>>
			Once your basket is empty, a few of the <<farm_text_many pig>> lay down. However, most of them are unsatisfied.
			<br><br>

			You don't know the way back, and you're worried about disturbing them, so you sit with your back against a tree. The <<farm_text_many pig>> get back up. However, instead of dispersing, they turn to you. They want something more.
			<br><br>

			<<farm_gen pig>>

			<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
				"Give too little," a <<farm_text pig>> says. "Very little. Still hungry. You satisfy."
			<<else>>
				You can tell they're still hungry. They look at you with lust.
			<</if>>
			<br><br>
		<</if>>

		<!--
			After feeding them, the PC will have the option to have consensual or non-consensual sex with the pigs that are unsatisfied.
		-->
		<<if hasSexStat("deviancy", 5)>>
			<<link [[Submit to them|Farm Woodland Pigs Reward]]>>
				<<set $sexstart to 1>>
				<<beastNEWinit _pigsUnsatisfied pig>>

				<<set $tempRewardHelpful to false>>
				<<set $tempTrueConsensual to false>>
				<<set $tempResponse to "submissive">>
				<<set $tempLocation to "woodland">>
			<</link>><<deviant5>>
			<br>
		<</if>>

		<<link [[Fight them off|Farm Woodland Pigs Reward]]>>
			<<set $molestationstart to 1>>
			<<beastNEWinit _pigsUnsatisfied pig>>

			<<set $tempRewardHelpful to false>>
			<<set $tempTrueConsensual to false>>
			<<set $tempResponse to "defiant">>
			<<set $tempLocation to "woodland">>
		<</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>

<<elseif $tempRewardType is "body">>
	<!--
		The PC will satisfy a pig with their body (+1 Pig's Respect). If the PC has good Science and Tending, they will recognize and reward a pig that was particularly helpful (+1 Pig's Respect).
	-->
	<<beastNEWinit 4 pig>>
	<<set $farm_work.pig.gender to $NPCList[0].gender>>
	
	You look among the <<farm_text_many pig>> gathered before you, deciding which one you'll offer your body to.
	<br><br>

	<!-- The PC should have a 50% of passing the Science check with a Science Grade of A. -->
	<<set _checkResults to [
		currentSkillValue("science") gte random(600, 800),
		currentSkillValue("tending") gte random(600, 800)
	]>>
	<!-- Going to hell for this lol -->
	<<if _checkResults[0] and _checkResults[1]>>

		<span class="teal">You recognize a <<farm_text pig>> who was particularly helpful.</span>
		<br><br>

		You close your basket and lie against it, guiding <<farm_him pig>> towards you. When <<farm_he pig>> reaches your waist, you hold <<farm_him pig>> there with your legs.
		<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>> "Reward?" <<farm_he pig>> asks.
		<<else>> It hesitates, unsure of your intentions.
		<</if>>
		<<deviancy5>>

		You address the rest of the <<farm_text_many pig>>.
		<br><br>

		<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
			"Um, hey!" you say.
			<<if $farm_work.pig.gender is "m">>
				"Mister <<farm_text pig>> helped me a lot today,
			<<else>>
				"Missus <<farm_text pig>> helped me a lot today,
			<</if>>
			so I wanted to give <<farm_him pig>> a reward! Next time, if you help me even more, we could do it instead." You release <<farm_him pig>>.
		<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
			"Hey!" you say.
			<<if $farm_work.pig.gender is "m">>
				"Mister <<farm_text pig>> here was very helpful today, so <<farm_he pig>> gets a big reward. Me! I saw you all eyeing me in the forest, so if you want join in, you'd better ask mister <<farm_text pig>> here for tips." You pull <<farm_him pig>> onto you.
			<<else>>
				"Missus <<farm_text pig>> here was very helpful today, so <<farm_he pig>> gets a big reward. Me! I saw you all eyeing me in the forest, so if you want join in, you'd better ask missus <<farm_text pig>> here for tips." You pull <<farm_him pig>> onto you.
			<</if>>
		<<else>>
			"Hey!" you say.
			<<if $farm_work.pig.gender is "m">>
				"Mister <<farm_text pig>> was very helpful today,
			<<else>>
				"Missus <<farm_text pig>> was very helpful today,
			<</if>>
			so <<farm_he pig>> gets to have some fun. If you want me too, then next time I'm around, I'll need you on your best behavior." You spread your legs.
		<</if>>
		<br><br>

		<span class="green">The <<farm_text_many pig>> are impressed by your discernment.</span><<farm_pigs 1>><<grespect>>
		<br><br>

		<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland Pigs Reward]]>>
			<<set $sexstart to 1>>

			<<set $tempRewardHelpful to true>>
			<<set $tempGenderHelpful to $farm_work.pig.gender>>
			<<set $tempTrueConsensual to false>>
			<<set $tempResponse to "submissive">>
			<<set $tempLocation to "woodland">>
		<</link>>
		<br>
	<<else>>
		<span class="teal">You have a hard time telling them apart,</span> and end up selecting one who looks vaguely familiar.
		<br><br>

		You close your basket and lie against it, guiding <<farm_him pig>> towards you. When <<farm_he pig>> reaches your waist, you hold <<farm_him pig>> there with your legs.
		<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>> "For me?" <<farm_he pig>> asks.
		<<else>> It presses against you, unsure of your intentions.
		<</if>>
		<<deviancy5>>

		You address the rest of the <<farm_text_many pig>>.
		<br><br>

		<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
			"Um, hey!" you say. "Thanks a lot for helping me today. I want to show you how much I appreciate it. Next time,
			if you help me even more, we could do it together instead." You release <<farm_him pig>> from your legs.
		<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
			"Hey!" you say. "You all were pretty helpful today.
			<<if $farm_work.pig.gender is "m">>
				As thanks, I'm letting mister <<farm_text pig>> here show you my thank you gift. I saw you all eyeing me in the
				forest, so if you want to join in, you'd better keep up the good work!" You pull <<farm_him pig>> onto you.
			<<else>>
				As thanks, I'm letting missus <<farm_text pig>> here show you my thank you gift. I saw you all eyeing me in the
				forest, so if you want to join in, you'd better keep up the good work!" You pull <<farm_him pig>> onto you.
			<</if>>
		<<else>>
			"Hey!" you say. "You all were fairly helpful today, and I know you all want a reward.
			<<if $farm_work.pig.gender is "m">>
				As thanks, mister <<farm_text pig>> and I will be putting on a show.
			<<else>>
				As thanks, missus <<farm_text pig>> and I will be putting on a show.
			<</if>>
			If you want me too, then next time I'm around, I'll need you on your best behavior." You spread your legs.
		<</if>>
		<br><br>

		The <<farm_text_many pig>> crowd around to watch you.
		<br><br>

		<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland Pigs Reward]]>>
			<<set $sexstart to 1>>

			<<set $tempRewardHelpful to false>>
			<<set $tempTrueConsensual to false>>
			<<set $tempResponse to "submissive">>
			<<set $tempLocation to "woodland">>
		<</link>>
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<<farm_gen pig>>

	<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
		"But..." You look into your basket. "But these are mine."
	<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
		"Hmph. You want these?" You wave around your basket. "Find them yourself."
	<<else>>
		"Sorry, but these are mine." You guard your basket.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>> Another <<farm_text pig>> responds. "Stupid human, not ask you. We take. You satisfy."
	<<else>> Your response only seems to aggravate them.
	<</if>>
	They advance on you, uncaring. You're deep in the woodland. There's nowhere to run.
	<br><br>

	<!-- Good luck. -->
	<<link [[Fight them off|Farm Woodland Pigs Reward]]>>
		<<set $molestationstart to 1>>
		<<beastNEWinit 5 pig>>

		<<set $tempRewardHelpful to false>>
		<<set $tempTrueConsensual to false>>
		<<set $tempResponse to "defiant">>
		<<set $tempLocation to "woodland">>
	<</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>


:: Farm Woodland Forage Reward
<<effects>>

<!-- rewardType can be "potato", "carrot", "apple", "body", or "nothing" -->
<!-- Reward Tradeoffs:
	Potato
		Pros:
			Can be grown in bulk and gives bonus Respect (+3).
		Cons:
			Requires a LOT of potatoes to satisfy the pigs.
			Takes a long time (20 min).
			Counts as a feeding action, and is disabled if the pigs are already fully fed.
	Carrot
		Pros:
			Can be grown in bulk.
			Needs less food that potatoes.
			Takes a short time (10 min).
		Cons:
			Only gives a small amount (+1) of Respect.
	Apple
		Pros:
			Gives bonus Respect if the PC has a good Housekeeping and Maths Skill (1-3 Respect in total).
			Needs much less food than potatoes.
		Cons:
			Must be manually gathered from the Forest.
			The extra Respect requires the PC to spend extra time feeding them (10-20 minutes in total).
	Body
		Pros:
			No food loss.
			A skill check can be passed to give +1 Respect.
			The pigs give up to +3 Respect at low Respect.
		Cons:
			The pigs only give +1 Respect at high Respect.
			Refusing or fighting off a pig at any point will make the following encounters non-consensual.
	Nothing
		Pros:
			No food loss. Lets you get -3 Pig's Respect.
		Cons:
			Nothing.
			The pigs won't harm you :)
			You should keep doing it :D
-->
<!--
	The in-game name of "carrot" is "wild_carrot".
	Quantities for "body" will be 2 at low Respect (<= -5), and 1 at normal respect (>5). "nothing" will be 0.
-->
<<if $tempRewardType is "potato" or $tempRewardType is "carrot" or $tempRewardType is "apple">>
	<<if $tempRewardType is "carrot">>
		<<set _rewardIcon to "wild_carrot">>
	<<else>>
		<<set _rewardIcon to $tempRewardType>>
	<</if>>

	<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
		"W-would you all want some <<pluralise $tempRewardQuantity $tempRewardType>>?" you ask.
	<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
		You think about what you have stocked. "Want some <<pluralise $tempRewardQuantity $tempRewardType>>?"
	<<else>>
		"How about some <<pluralise $tempRewardQuantity $tempRewardType>>?" you say.
	<</if>>

	<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
		"Food?" "Reward"? "$tempRewardType?" "Food?" "<<pShe>> give?" "Reward?"
	<<else>>
		They oink to each other.
	<</if>>
	<<switch $tempRewardType>>
		<<case "potato">>
			You think they recognized the word "potato." They start shuffling back to the farm.
		<<case "carrot">>
			You think they recognized the word "carrot." They start walking back to the farm.
		<<case "apple">>
			You think they recognized the word "apple." They start trotting back to the farm.
	<</switch>>
	<br><br>

	After leaving the woodland, you head to the storehouse.

	<<switch $tempRewardType>>
		<<case "potato">>
			<<pass 20>>

			You fill your basket with potatoes, then pour them into the pen. You have to make several trips, the <<farm_text_many pig>> hungry from all of the exertion. By the end, they rest on their sides.
			<<set $farm_work.pigs_fed += 1>><<physique 2>>
			<br><br>

			<span class="green">You think they found it filling.</span><<ggrespect>><<farm_pigs 3>>
		<<case "carrot">>
			<<pass 10>>

			You fill your basket with carrots, then pour them into the pen. You make a few trips, the <<farm_text_many pig>> crunching them for longer than you think is necessary. When they're done, they wander away from the fence.
			<<physique 1>>
			<br><br>

			You think they enjoyed the snack.<<grespect>><<farm_pigs 1>>
		<<case "apple">>
			You fill your basket with apples and head back to the pen, a small crowd having formed by the fence. You're worried they may injure themselves if you just pour them in, so you try to split them evenly.
			<br><br>

			<!--
				The Apple Strudel recipe requires the PC to cut apples, and needs Housekeeping Level 2 (aka Housekeeping C) to learn it.

				Accurately cutting the apples so that each pig gets roughly the same amount will require a Maths Skill of A, because the PC will need to estimate the fraction of each apple to give to each pig.
			-->
			<<if currentSkillValue("housekeeping") gte 400 and $mathstrait gte 3>>
				<!-- Takes extra time to feed them properly. -->
				<<pass 10>>

				You spend some time counting up the <<farm_text_many pig>> because they keep moving around. You then cut the apples so that <span class="teal">each <<farm_text_neutral pig>> gets roughly the same amount.</span>
				<br><br>

				<span class="green">The <<farm_text_many pig>> are very happy with your efforts.</span><<ggrespect>><<farm_pigs 3>>
			<<elseif currentSkillValue("housekeeping") gte 400>>
				<!-- Takes a little extra time to cut the pieces. -->
				<<pass 5>>

				You try to count how many <<farm_text_many pig>> there are, <span class="teal">but the math makes you dizzy.</span> You settle for an estimate instead. By the time you're nearly done, you realize your pieces were a little <<if random(1, 2) is 1>> too small. <<else>> too large. <</if>>
				<br><br>

				<span class="green">The <<farm_text_many pig>> appreciate your efforts.</span><<grespect>><<farm_pigs 2>>
			<<else>>
				You're worried about <span class="teal">cutting yourself with a the kitchen knife,</span> so you hand them out individually. Some <<farm_text_many pig>> inevitably get less than others.
				<br><br>

				The <<farm_text_many pig>> root around for leftovers.<<grespect>><<farm_pigs 1>>
			<</if>>
			<!-- Default amount of time. -->
			<<pass 10>>
	<</switch>>
	<br><br>

	By the end, you feed them a total of
	<span class="green"><<foodstufficon _rewardIcon>> $tempRewardQuantity <<pluralise $tempRewardQuantity $tempRewardType>>.</span>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Farm Work]]>>
		<<endWoodlandForage>>
	<</link>>
	<br>

<<elseif $tempRewardType is "body">>
	<!-- Should not be possible to reach this branch without bestiality being enabled or the farm pigs being monsters. -->
	<!--
		The PC will satisfy a pig with their body (+1 Pig's Respect). If the PC has good Science and Tending, they will recognize and reward a pig that was particularly helpful (+1 Pig's Respect).
	-->
	<<if $farm.beasts.pigs gte 5>>
		<<set _pigsUnsatisfied to 1>>
	<<elseif $farm.beasts.pigs gte -5>>
		<<set _pigsUnsatisfied to 2>>
	<<else>>
		<<set _pigsUnsatisfied to 3>>
	<</if>>

	<<beastNEWinit _pigsUnsatisfied pig>>
	<<set $farm_work.pig.gender to $NPCList[0].gender>>

	You look among the <<farm_text_many pig>> gathered before you, deciding which one you'll reward.
	<br><br>

	<!-- The PC should have a 50% of passing the Science check with a Science Grade of A. -->
	<<set _checkResults to [
		currentSkillValue("science") gte random(600, 800),
		currentSkillValue("tending") gte random(600, 800)
	]>>
	<!-- Going to hell for this lol -->
	<<if _checkResults[0] and _checkResults[1]>>
		<span class="teal">You recognize a <<farm_text pig>> who was particularly helpful.</span>
		<br><br>

		You close your basket and lie against it, guiding <<farm_him pig>> towards you. When <<farm_he pig>> reaches your waist, you hold <<farm_him pig>> there with your legs.
		<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>"Reward?" <<farm_he pig>> asks.<<else>>It hesitates, unsure of your intentions.<</if>>
		<<deviancy5>>

		You address the rest of the <<farm_text_many pig>>.
		<br><br>

		<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
			"Um, hey!" you say.
			<<if $farm_work.pig.gender is "m">>
				"Mister <<farm_text pig>> helped me a lot today,
			<<else>>
				"Missus <<farm_text pig>> helped me a lot today,
			<</if>>
			so I wanted to give <<farm_him pig>> a reward! Next time, if you help me even more, we could do it instead." You release <<farm_him pig>>.
		<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
			"Hey!" you say.
			<<if $farm_work.pig.gender is "m">>
				"Mister <<farm_text pig>> here was very helpful today, so <<farm_he pig>> gets a big reward. Me! I saw you all eyeing me in the forest, so if you want join in, you'd better ask mister <<farm_text pig>> here for tips." You pull <<farm_him pig>> onto you.
			<<else>>
				"Missus <<farm_text pig>> here was very helpful today, so <<farm_he pig>> gets a big reward. Me! I saw you all eyeing me in the forest, so if you want join in, you'd better ask missus <<farm_text pig>> here for tips." You pull <<farm_him pig>> onto you.
			<</if>>
		<<else>>
			"Hey!" you say.
			<<if $farm_work.pig.gender is "m">>
				"Mister <<farm_text pig>> was very helpful today,
			<<else>>
				"Missus <<farm_text pig>> was very helpful today,
			<</if>>
			so <<farm_he pig>> gets to have some fun. If you want me too, then next time I'm around, I'll need you on your best behavior." You spread your legs.
		<</if>>
		<br><br>

		<span class="green">The <<farm_text_many pig>> are impressed by your discernment.</span><<farm_pigs 1>><<grespect>>
		<br><br>

		<!-- This is the only instance of non-forced consensual sex betwen the PC and a pig, where the PC actually has the option to ask the pig to stop. -->
		<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland Pigs Reward]]>>
			<<set $sexstart to 1>>

			<<set $tempRewardHelpful to true>>
			<<set $tempGenderHelpful to $farm_work.pig.gender>>
			<<set $tempTrueConsensual to true>>
			<<set $tempResponse to "submissive">>
			<<set $tempLocation to "treeline">>
		<</link>>
		<br>
	<<else>>
		<span class="teal">You have a hard time telling them apart,</span> and end up selecting one who looks vaguely familiar.
		<br><br>

		You close your basket and lie against it, guiding <<farm_him pig>> towards you. When <<farm_he pig>> crawls up to
		your waist, you hold <<farm_him pig>> there with your legs.
		<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>"For me?" <<farm_he pig>> asks.<<else>>It presses against you, unsure of your intentions.<</if>>
		<<deviancy5>>

		You address the rest of the <<farm_text_many pig>>.
		<br><br>

		<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
			"Um, hey!" you say. "Thanks a lot for helping me today. I want to show you how much I appreciate it. Next time,
			if you help me even more, we could do it together instead." You release <<farm_him pig>> from your legs.
		<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
			"Hey!" you say. "You all were pretty helpful today.
			<<if $farm_work.pig.gender is "m">>
				As thanks, I'm letting mister <<farm_text pig>> here show you my thank you gift. I saw you all eyeing me in the
				forest, so if you want to join in, you'd better keep up the good work!" You pull <<farm_him pig>> onto you.
			<<else>>
				As thanks, I'm letting missus <<farm_text pig>> here show you my thank you gift. I saw you all eyeing me in the
				forest, so if you want to join in, you'd better keep up the good work!" You pull <<farm_him pig>> onto you.
			<</if>>
		<<else>>
			"Hey!" you say. "You all were fairly helpful today, and I know you all want a reward.
			<<if $farm_work.pig.gender is "m">>
				As thanks, mister <<farm_text pig>> and I will be putting on a show.
			<<else>>
				As thanks, missus <<farm_text pig>> and I will be putting on a show.
			<</if>>
			If you want me too, then next time I'm around, I'll need you on your best behavior." You spread your legs.
		<</if>>
		<br><br>

		The <<farm_text_many pig>> crowd around to watch you.
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland Pigs Reward]]>>
			<<set $sexstart to 1>>

			<<set $tempRewardHelpful to false>>
			<<set $tempTrueConsensual to false>>
			<<set $tempResponse to "submissive">>
			<<set $tempLocation to "treeline">>
		<</link>>
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<<farm_pigs -3>>
	<<if $farm.beasts.pigs gte -5 or not ($settings.bestialityEnabled or $farm_work.pig.monster)>>
		They consider you, then snort and trot away.
		<br><br>

		<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland]]>>
			<<endWoodlandForage>>
		<</link>>
		<br>
	<<else>>
		<<beastNEWinit 1 pig>>
		<<set $farm_work.pig.gender to $NPCList[0].gender>>

		They consider you, then snort and trot away.
		<br><br>

		As they do, a <<farm_text pig>> stays behind.

		<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
			<<if random(1, 3) is 1>>
				"Not enough. Not satisfy." <<farm_He pig>> says. "Stupid human need breed."
			<<elseif random(1, 2) is 1>>
				"More breed," <<farm_he pig>> says. "Stupid human reward."
			<<else>>
				"No reward. Lie," <<farm_he pig>> says. "Stupid human can satisfy."
			<</if>>
		<<else>>
			<<farm_He pig>> growls at you, blocking your path.
		<</if>>

		The <<farm_text_many pig>> turn around at the sound of <<farm_his pig>> voice. You try to move around <<farm_him pig>>, but <<farm_he pig>> moves between you and the farm. You look around. The other <<farm_text_many pig>> don't try to stop you, but they also don't try to stop the <<farm_text pig>>.
		<br><br>

		<<link [[Fight <<farm_him pig>> off|Farm Woodland Pigs Reward]]>>
			<<set $molestationstart to 1>>

			<<set $tempRewardHelpful to false>>
			<<set $tempTrueConsensual to false>>
			<<set $tempResponse to "defiant">>
			<<set $tempLocation to "treeline">>
		<</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
<</if>>


:: Farm Woodland Pigs Reward

<<if $sexstart is 1 or $molestationstart is 1>>
	<<if $tempLocation is "treeline">>
		<span class="green">You are at the edge of the woodland. Alex might be able to hear you.</span>
		<br><br>
	<<elseif $tempLocation is "woodland">>
		<span class="red">You are deep in the woodland. Alex will not be able to hear your cries.</span>
		<br><br>
	<<else>>
		ERROR (Farm Woodland Pigs Reward): Invalid tempLocation "$tempLocation".
	<</if>>

	<<if $sexstart is 1>>
		<<set $sexstart to 0>>
		<<set $consensual to 1>>

		<<deviancy5>>
		<<consensual>>
		<<neutral 1>>
		<<set $position to "missionary">>
	<<else>>
		<<set $molestationstart to 0>>
		<<set $consensual to 0>>

		<<controlloss>>
		<<violence 1>>
		<<neutral 1>>
		<<molested>>
	<</if>>

	<<beastCombatInit>>
	<<beastTrainGenerate>>

	<<if $tempLocation is "treeline" and Time.betweenHours(5, 20)>>
		<<enable_rescue>>
	<<else>>
		<<set $rescue to 0>>
	<</if>>

	<<farm_trust pig>>

	<!--
		Submissive starts has no change.
		Defiant starts with increased Anger and decreased Trust.
	-->
	<<if $tempResponse is "defiant">>
		<<set $enemyanger += 40>>
		<<set $enemytrust -= 40>>
	<</if>>

	<<if $tempTrueConsensual>>
		<<set $noFinish to 0>>
	<<else>>
		<<set $noFinish to 1>>
	<</if>>
<</if>>

<<effects>>
<<effectsman>>
<<alarmstate>>
<<beast $enemyno>>
<br>

<<if $consensual is 1>>The other <<farm_text_many pig>> crowd around you, eager to see you moan.
<<else>>The other <<farm_text_many pig>> crowd around you, eager to see you squeal.
<</if>>

<!-- Fungi stealing checks for if the PC non-consensually "rewards" the pigs deep in the woodland. -->
<<if $tempLocation is "woodland" and $consensual is 0>>
<!-- PC effectively loses 1 fungi per turn. -->
	<<for $_i = 0; $_i < 5; $_i++>>
		<<if ($tempBasket[0] + $tempBasket[1] gt 0) and random(1, 5) is 1>>
			<<if ($tempBasket[1] is 0) or ($tempBasket[0] gt 0 and $tempBasket[1] gt 0 and random(1, 2) is 1)>>
				<<set _foodTarget to "mushroom">>
				<<set $tempBasket[0] -= 1>>
				<<set $foodstuff["mushroom"].amount -= 1>>
			<<else>>
				<<set _foodTarget to "truffle">>
				<<set $tempBasket[1] -= 1>>
				<<set $foodstuff["truffle"].amount -= 1>>
			<</if>>

			<!-- There are much more than 5 pigs in the audience, so trying to track them all is impractical. Instead, re-roll the pig's gender every time the pigs succeed at stealing from the PC's basket. -->
			<br><br>
			<<farm_gen pig>>
			A <<farm_text pig $farm_work.pig.gender>> munches on a _foodTarget from your basket.
		<</if>>
	<</for>>
<</if>>

<br><br>
<<stateman>>
<br><br>
<<actionsman>>

<<if _combatend>>
	<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Farm Woodland Pigs Reward Finish]]>><</link>></span><<nexttext>>
<<else>>
	<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Farm Woodland Pigs Reward]]>><</link>></span><<nexttext>>
<</if>>

:: Farm Woodland Pigs Reward Finish

<!-- Fighting off the pig will remove the option for consensual sex. -->
<<if $enemyhealth lte 0>>
	<<beastwound>>
	The <<farm_text pig>> backs away from you, cowed. The others make room after seeing how you fought.<<farm_pigs 1>><<grespect>>
	<br><br>

	<<tearful>> you try to push yourself back up.

	<<if $combatTrain.length gt 0>>
		<<combatTrainAdvance>>
		<<set $farm_work.pig.gender to $NPCList[0].gender>>

		As you do, another <<farm_text pig>> approaches you.

		<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
			<<if random(1, 3) is 1>>
				"Not enough. Not satisfy." <<farm_He pig>> says. "Need breed more."
			<<elseif random(1, 2) is 1>>
				"More breed," <<farm_he pig>> says. "Too pretty."
			<<else>>
				"Too pretty," <<farm_he pig>> says. "We not satisfied."
			<</if>>
		<<else>>
			<<farm_He pig>> paws at the ground.
		<</if>>
		Despite your display, you can tell <<farm_he pig>> thinks you're worth the risk.
		<br><br>

		You look around. The other <<farm_text_many pig>> seem just as lustful. How many more will you need to fight off?
		<br><br>

		<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland Pigs Reward]]>>
			<<set $consensual to 0>>
			<<set $tempTrueConsensual to false>>
			<<set $tempResponse to "defiant">>
		<</link>>
		<br>
	<<else>>
		<<clotheson>>
		<<endcombat>>

		<<if $tempLocation is "treeline">>
			They don't stop you. You grab your basket and start walking back towards the farm.
			<br><br>
		<<else>>
			<<set _passTime to random(30, 40)>>
			<<pass _passTime>>
			<!-- Pigs immediately flee to the farm if they are fought off, but since they don't directly guide the
				player back, the player needs to spend some extra time orienting themselves. -->
			The <<farm_text_many pig>> have had enough of your violence. One runs away. You clench your fist. Another flees. And then another. Soon, only stragglers remain. Most of the <<farm_text_many pig>> flee in the same direction. You suspect they're running back to the farm. You follow them.
			<br><br>

			<!-- Tending skill of B. -->
			You come across many different animal tracks on your way back.
			<<if $sciencetrait gte 3>>
				<span class="green">You remember your lessons from science class.</span>
				You follow the pig prints back to the farm.
			<<else>>
				<<pass 20>>
				The indents all look the same. You spend some time going in circles, until at last, you see some familiar
				buildings through the treeline.
			<</if>>
			<br><br>

			Throughout it all, you find yourself wondering what exactly just happened.
			<br><br>

			Where did they take you?
			<<stress 6>><<gstress>>
			<br><br>
			<br><br>

			Why were they so organized?
			<<stress 6>><<gstress>>
			<br><br>
			<br><br>
			<br><br>

			Does anyone know?
			<<stress 6>><<gstress>>
			<br><br>
			<br><br>
			<br><br>
			<br><br>
			<br><br>
			<br><br>

			Will anyone believe you?
			<<stress 6>><<gstress>>
			<br><br>
		<</if>>

		<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland]]>>
			<<endWoodlandForage>>
		<</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>

<<elseif $enemyarousal gte $enemyarousalmax>>
	<<beastejaculation>>

	The <<farm_text pig>> climbs off you, satisfied.

	<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
		The others cheer.
		<!-- +1 Respect if done consensually. -1 Respect if non-consensual. -->
		<<if $consensual is 1>>
			<<grespect>><<farm_pigs 1>>
		<<else>>
			<<lrespect>><<farm_pigs -1>>
		<</if>>
		<br>

		<<if $consensual is 1>>
			<<if random(1, 2) is 2>>
				"<<pShe>> so breedable."
			<<else>>
				"You see <<phim>> face?"
			<</if>>
			<br>

			<<if random(1, 2) is 2>>
				"You should been rougher."
			<<else>>
				"Can be rougher next time."
			<</if>>
			<br>

			<<if random(1, 2) is 2>>
				"Can we keep <<phim>>?"
			<<else>>
				"We can breed more if want stay."
			<</if>>

		<<else>>
			<<if random(1, 2) is 2>>
				"Not so great now."
			<<else>>
				"I hope <<pshe>> know place."
			<</if>>
			<br>

			<<if random(1, 2) is 2>>
				"You should been rougher."
			<<else>>
				"Can be rougher next time."
			<</if>>
			<br>

			<<if random(1, 2) is 2>>
				"We keep <<phim>> here?"
			<<else>>
				"I bet <<pshe>> like that."
			<</if>>
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		The others crowd around it. They sniff and lick it, then turn back to you.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<tearful>> you try to push yourself back up.

	<<if $combatTrain.length gt 0>>
		<<combatTrainAdvance>>
		<<set $farm_work.pig.gender to $NPCList[0].gender>>

		As you do, another <<farm_text pig>> approaches you.

		<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
			<<if random(1, 3) is 1>>
				"Not enough. Not satisfy." <<farm_He pig>> says. "Need breed more."
			<<elseif random(1, 2) is 1>>
				"More breed," <<farm_he pig>> says. "Reward too little."
			<<else>>
				"Reward too few," <<farm_he pig>> says. "We not satisfied."
			<</if>>
		<<else>>
			<<farm_He pig>> paws at the ground. You can tell <<farm_he pig>> also wants to mate.
		<</if>>
		<br><br>

		<<if $tempRewardHelpful>>
			<<set $tempRewardHelpful to false>>
			The <<farm_text pig $tempGenderHelpful>> you had sex with moves to block <<farm_him pig>>. "No. You not helpful. No reward." The <<farm_text_many pig>> stare at each other. They lunge at each other and start wrestling on the
			ground. The other <<farm_text_many pig>> watch in silence.
			<br><br>

			<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland Pigs Helpful Fight]]>>
				<<set $tempTrueConsensual to false>>
			<</link>>
		<<else>>
			You look around. The other <<farm_text_many pig>> seem just as lustful. How many more will you need to satisfy?
			<br><br>

			<!-- Does not make following encounters consensual, if they are already non-consensual. Pigs will just start off less angry. -->
			<<if hasSexStat("deviancy", 5)>>
				<<link [[Submit to them|Farm Woodland Pigs Reward]]>>
					<<set $tempTrueConsensual to false>>
					<<set $tempResponse to "submissive">>
				<</link>><<deviant5>>
			<br>
			<</if>>

			<<link [[Fight them off|Farm Woodland Pigs Reward]]>>
				<<set $consensual to 0>>
				<<set $tempTrueConsensual to false>>
				<<set $tempResponse to "defiant">>
			<</link>>
			<br>
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		They don't stop you.
		
		<<clotheson>>
		<<endcombat>>

		<<if $tempLocation is "treeline" and $consensual>>
			You grab your basket and start walking back towards the farm.
		<<elseif $tempLocation is "treeline">>
			You grab your basket and stagger back towards the farm.
		<<elseif $tempLocation is "woodland" and $consensual>>
			<<set _passTime to random(30, 40)>>
			<<pass _passTime>>
			<!-- Grand Pig Conspiracy when? -->
			Done with fucking you, the <<farm_text_many pig>> laze about on the earth. Looking around, it's clear you only had sex with a small number of those who had gathered here.
			<br><br>

			<span class="red">You wonder why they seem so organized.</span>
			<<stress 6>><<gstress>>
			<br><br>

			You don't know the way back, so you wait for them to get up.
			<<if $tempRewardType is "basket">>
				Some <<farm_text_many pig>> approach you during this time, giving you a lick or a nuzzle for the meal.
			<</if>>
			A few of them still look at you with lustful eyes, but the others form a ring of sorts that stops them from
			approaching.
			<br><br>

			<span class="red">It seems like they think you've paid your due.</span>
			<<stress 6>><<gstress>>
			<br><br>

			<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
				<<if $tempRewardType is "basket">>
					"Body good, thank for meal," a <<farm_text pig>> says. "We go back now." You follow them.
				<<else>>
					"Body good," a <<farm_text pig>> says. "We go back now." You follow them.
				<</if>>
			<<else>>
				Eventually, they get up and start trotting somewhere. You follow them.
			<</if>>
		<<else>>
			<<set _passTime to random(30, 40)>>
			<<pass _passTime>>
			<span class="red">You ache all over.</span>
			<<trauma 6>><<stress 6>><<gtrauma>><<gstress>>
			<br><br>

			Done with fucking you, the <<farm_text_many pig>> laze about on the earth. Looking around, it's clear you only had sex with a small number of those who had gathered here.
			<br><br>

			<span class="red">You wonder why they seem so organized.</span>
			<<trauma 6>><<stress 6>><<gtrauma>><<gstress>>
			<br><br>

			You don't know the way back, so you wait for them to get up. A few of them still look at you with lustful eyes, but the others form a ring of sorts that stops them from approaching.
			<br><br>

			<span class="red">It seems like they think you've paid your due.</span>
			<<trauma 6>><<stress 6>><<gtrauma>><<gstress>>
			<br><br>

			<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
				<<if $tempRewardType is "basket" or $tempBasket[0] + $tempBasket[1] is 0>>
					"Thank for meal, fucktoy," a <<farm_text pig>> says. "We leave." Hesitantly, you follow them.
				<<else>>
					"Fucktoy learn good lesson," a <<farm_text pig>> says. "We leave." Hesitantly, you follow them.
				<</if>>
			<<else>>
				Eventually, they get up and start trotting somewhere. They leer at you as they go. Hesitatntly, you follow them.
			<</if>>
		<</if>>
		<br><br>

		<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland]]>>
			<<endWoodlandForage>>
		<</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>

<<elseif $alarm is 1 and $rescue gte 1>><<set $rescued += 1>>
	"I'm coming!" It's Alex. The <<farm_text_many pig>> back away from you at the sound. They start fleeing into the undergrowth.
	<<farm_pigs -3>><<llrespect>>
	<br><br>

	<<clotheson>>
	<<endcombat>>

	<<npc Alex>><<person1>>
	Alex arrives at the edge of the woodland. <<He>> pushes through the foliage and helps you to your feet. Seeing the pig prints all around and on you, he laughs. "Pigs can be like that," <<he>> says. "If all else fails, don't be afraid to lay down the law."

	<<if $exposed gte 1>>
		<<glust>><<npcincr Alex lust 1>>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland]]>>
		<<endWoodlandForage>>
	<</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<!--
		Consensual "Ask to stop" edge case. Honestly such an edge case that you could make an argument that there should be a Feat awarded for achieving it. Would be relatively easy to achieve though. Just obscure.
	-->
	The <<farm_text pig>> slowly climbs off of you.
	<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
		<<farm_He pig>> whines. "Why no mate? I good. We good. Help you."
	<<else>>
		It whines. It paws at your leg, pleading with its eyes.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<tearful>> you push yourself off the ground.
	<br><br>

	<<clotheson>>
	<<endcombat>>

	<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
		As you walk away, the other pigpeople jeer at you.
	<<else>>
		As you walk away, you hear squeals and oinks behind you.
	<</if>>
	It's clear you've agitated them.<<farm_pigs -3>><<llrespect>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland]]>>
		<<endWoodlandForage>>
	<</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>


<!--
	There is a potential bug where the PC rewards the helpful pig in the Woodland, while there is only 1 pig left to satisfy. This would cause the helpful pig to save the PC, and the text would say the PC is able to walk out of the Woodland on their own.

	This situation is currently impossible because the "Farm Woodland Forage Reward Extreme" event starts at 4 unsatisfied pigs, and the "helpfulPig" event can only triggers one time after the first pig is satisfied.

	However, if the Woodland events get changed in the future, this edge case may need need to be handled.
-->
:: Farm Woodland Pigs Helpful Fight
<<effects>>

<!--
	Your pig has a 40% chance of winning you the +1 Respect and -1 pig. Your power of horni fills it with determination! Unfortunately it just had sex with you, and you milked it RATHER good.
-->
<<if random(1, 5) lte 3>>
	At last, the other <<farm_text pig>> presses your <<farm_text pig $tempGenderHelpful>> into the dirt. The <<farm_text_many pig>> look between you and your <<farm_text pig $tempGenderHelpful>>.
	<<stress 6>><<gstress>>
	<br><br>

	<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
		Panting, <<farm_he pig $tempGenderHelpful>> looks up at the other <<farm_text_many pig>>. "No... helpful. No... reward."
	<<else>>
		It looks tired, struggling underneath the other pig, but still finds rooms in its lungs to muster out a whine.
	<</if>>
	Your <<farm_text pig $tempGenderHelpful>> won't be able to fight another <<farm_text_neutral pig>>, if they insist.
	<br><br>

	<!--
		While your horni savior may have lost, their valiant struggle gives them a 50% chance of convincing the other pigs to be nicer to you! If you lose the coinflip, #SkillIssue.
	-->
	<<if random(1, 2) is 1>>
		<<set $phase to 0>>
		<<combatTrainAdvance>>
	<<else>>
		<!-- If the helpful pig loses, AND fails to persuade the other pigs, a new pig will speak out but the original pig will advance on the PC. -->
		<<set $phase to 1>>
	<</if>>

<<else>>
	At last, your <<farm_text pig $tempGenderHelpful>> presses the other <<farm_text pig>> into the dirt.
	<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
		Panting, <<farm_he pig $tempGenderHelpful>> looks at the other <<farm_text_many pig>> and repeats himself.
		"No helpful. No reward."
	<<else>>
		It looks tired, but still manages a growl towards the other pigs.
	<</if>>
	<<farm_pigs 1>><<grespect>>
	<br><br>

	The other <<farm_text_many pig>> look between you and your <<farm_text pig $tempGenderHelpful>>. You can tell your <<farm_text pig $tempGenderHelpful>> is too tired to fight another <<farm_text_neutral pig>>, if they insist.

	<<set $phase to 0>>
	<<combatTrainAdvance>>
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland Pigs Helpful Results]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Farm Woodland Pigs Helpful Results
<<effects>>

<<if $combatTrain.length gt 0>>
	<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
		They respect <<farm_his pig $tempGenderHelpful>> statement.
	<<else>>
		They respect its efforts.
	<</if>>

	The other <<farm_text_many pig>> start trickling back into the woodland, looking for other things to interest them.
	<br><br>

	<<clotheson>>
	<<endcombat>>

	Picking up your basket, you find your <<farm_text pig $tempGenderHelpful>> standing in front of you.

	<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
		"Good sex," <<farm_he pig $tempGenderHelpful>> says. "Wanted to thank."
	<<else>>
		It nuzzles and licks your legs.
	<</if>>
	<<lstress>><<stress -6>>
	<br><br>

	You give your <<farm_text pig $tempGenderHelpful>> a pat on the head, then start heading back towards the farm.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland]]>>
		<<endWoodlandForage>>
	<</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<!-- BROTHER. MAY I HAVE SOME OATS?!?!?! -->
	<!--
		The branches of potential pigs that can enter this situation is kind of scuffed.

		They are:
		1. Helpful Wins ("combatTrainAdvance" called. New pig talks. New pig advances on PC.)
		2. Helpful Loses, Persuasion Successful ("combatTrainAdvance" called. New pig talks. New pig advances on PC.)
		3. Helpful Loses, Persuasion Failed ("combatTrainAdvance" not called. New pig talks. Same pig advances on PC.)

		Would make sense in the 3rd case if the same pig starts out extra tired from wrestling with the helpful pig, but there isn't a clean way to convert that stat into Enemy Pain / Arousal / Anger / Trust.
	-->
	<<if $phase is 0>>
		<<set $farm_work.pig.gender to $NPCList[0].gender>>
	<<else>>
		<<farm_gen pig>>
	<</if>>

	Another <<farm_text pig>> steps forward.
	<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
		<<if random(1, 3) is 1>>
			"Still not enough. Still not satisfy." <<farm_He pig>> says. "Need breed more."
		<<elseif random(1, 2) is 1>>
			"Still more breed," <<farm_he pig>> says. "Reward too little."
		<<else>>
			"Still reward too few," <<farm_he pig>> says. "We not satisfy."
		<</if>>
		The other pigpeople murmur in agreement. Your <<farm_text pig $tempGenderHelpful>> looks at you, then deflates. "Sorry. Tried. Can't protect," <<farm_he pig $tempGenderHelpful>> says. <<farm_He pig $tempGenderHelpful>> watches, remorseful, as the <<farm_text pig>> approaches you.
	<<else>>
		It oinks at your pig, then growls at you. The other pigs growl as well. Your pig looks at you, whining. The other pigs begin to growl at it. When another pig steps towards it, it deflates. It looks on, remorseful, as the other pig approaches you.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<!-- Shouldn't be possible for a PC to reach this scene without already having Deviancy 5, but just in case. -->
	<<if hasSexStat("deviancy", 5)>>
		<<link [[Submit to them|Farm Woodland Pigs Reward]]>>
			<<set $tempTrueConsensual to false>>
			<<set $tempResponse to "submissive">>
		<</link>><<deviant5>>
		<br>
	<</if>>

	<<link [[Fight <<farm_him pig>> off|Farm Woodland Pigs Reward]]>>
		<<set $consensual to 0>>
		<<set $tempTrueConsensual to false>>
		<<set $tempResponse to "defiant">>
	<</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Farm Woodland Pigs Scold
<<effects>>

<<if $tendingSuccess>>
	<<if $tempPosition is "standing">>
		<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
			"Away!" you say, <span class="green">your voice firm and sure.</span> The <<farm_text pig>> releases you, chastened, and goes back to foraging among the trees.
			<<farm_pigs 1>><<grespect>>
		<<else>>
			"Down!" you say, <span class="green">your voice firm and sure.</span> The pig drops to the ground, chastened, and goes back to rooting among the trees.
			<<farm_pigs 1>><<grespect>>
		<</if>>
	<<elseif $tempPosition is "prone">>
		<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
			"Away!" you say, <span class="green">your voice firm and sure.</span> The <<farm_text pig>> backs away from you, chastened, and goes back to foraging among the trees.
			<<farm_pigs 1>><<grespect>>
		<<else>>
			"Back!" you say, <span class="green">your voice firm and sure.</span> The pig backs away from you, chastened, and goes back to rooting among the trees.
			<<farm_pigs 1>><<grespect>>
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		ERROR (Farm Woodland Pigs Scold): Invalid tempPosition "$tempPosition".
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Continue|Farm Woodland Forage]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<if ($tempPosition is "prone") or ($farm.beasts.pigs lt -5 and $rng gte 51)>>
		<<if $tempPosition is "standing">>
			<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
				"A-away!" you say, but <span class="red">your voice shakes,</span> and the <<farm_text pig>> pays you no heed. <<farm_He pig>> pulls you to the ground.
				<<farm_pigs -1>><<trauma 6>><<stress 6>><<lrespect>><<gtrauma>><<gstress>>
			<<else>>
				"D-down!" you say, but <span class="red">your voice shakes,</span> and the pig pays you no heed. It forces you to the ground.
				<<farm_pigs -1>><<trauma 6>><<stress 6>><<lrespect>><<gtrauma>><<gstress>>
